From: yanan.he <yanan.he@linux.alibaba.com>
Subject: [PATCH] python: replace PyEval_CallObject/CallMethod removed in 3.13

Python 3.13 removed PyEval_CallObject and PyEval_CallMethod from the C
API (deprecated since 3.9). libxml2 2.9.14's bindings still call them;
they compile only as implicit declarations and the resulting
libxml2mod.so has undefined symbols, so `import libxml2` fails:
"undefined symbol: PyEval_CallObject". This breaks itstool-native
do_configure ("Python module libxml2 is needed").

PyObject_CallObject / PyObject_CallMethod are drop-in equivalents
available in every supported Python version (same call semantics).

Upstream-Status: Backport [fixed differently in >= 2.10]
Signed-off-by: yanan.he <yanan.he@linux.alibaba.com>
---
 python/libxml.c | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++--------------------
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)

--- a/python/libxml.c	2026-07-31 12:17:02.114496807 +0800
+++ b/python/libxml.c	2026-07-31 12:17:02.114496807 +0800
@@ -257,7 +257,7 @@
 #endif
     file = (PyObject *) context;
     if (file == NULL) return(-1);
-    ret = PyEval_CallMethod(file, (char *) "close", (char *) "()");
+    ret = PyObject_CallMethod(file, (char *) "close", (char *) "()");
     if (ret != NULL) {
 	Py_DECREF(ret);
     }
@@ -287,7 +287,7 @@
 #endif
